# Copy to .env for local development. Never commit real values.
# Real credentials, tokens, and connection strings must never be committed to this repository.

# --- Database (see docs/architecture/database-design.md) ---
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://localhost:5432/expense_reconciliation_dev

# --- AI provider (see docs/architecture/ai-boundary.md) ---
# The AI layer only ever produces proposals; it never writes authoritative financial state.
# Leave ANTHROPIC_API_KEY blank and every AI operation refuses by name rather than degrading
# quietly: classification and receipt extraction report that no provider is configured, and
# every payment can still be classified by hand from the payment workspace.
#
# What is sent when it is set: an already-redacted payload, checked by
# `ai.assertPayloadSanitized` before the transport sees it. Never an account number, a UPI id,
# a real name, or a document's bytes (docs/security/security-model.md).
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# Optional. Defaults to the model named in src/integrations/anthropic/transport.ts.
ANTHROPIC_MODEL=

# --- Splitwise integration (see docs/product/overview.md, Splitwise section) ---
# An API key or OAuth access token for the Splitwise account to compare against, plus that
# account's own Splitwise user id (the value stored on `people.splitwise_user_id` for the
# ledger's user). Both are needed together; either alone leaves the adapter unconfigured.
#
# Leave blank and every Splitwise call refuses rather than resolving empty: an audit against an
# unreadable account is recorded as an INCOMPLETE check, never as agreement (ADR-0046).
#
# Reads are compared, never trusted; writes are first-sync only. Do not point this at a
# production Splitwise account while developing.
SPLITWISE_API_KEY=
SPLITWISE_USER_ID=

# --- Evidence storage (see docs/security/security-model.md, ADR-0033) ---
# Where receipt images and other evidence documents are written in development. Documents are
# content-addressed (sha256/<digest>.<ext>), so nothing about a merchant or a filename appears
# in a path. Gitignored: no real financial document belongs in this repository.
EVIDENCE_STORAGE_PATH=./local-data/evidence

# --- Integration tests (see docs/decisions/0017-integration-test-database.md) ---
# Point this at a real PostgreSQL instance to run the integration suite against a server.
# Left unset, the suite runs against PGlite (PostgreSQL compiled to WebAssembly, in-process),
# so it executes everywhere without Docker. CI sets this to a Postgres service container.
#
# The suite creates one throwaway database per test file and drops it afterwards, because
# Vitest runs files in parallel. The role therefore needs CREATE DATABASE, and the server's
# `postgres` maintenance database must be reachable.
TEST_DATABASE_URL=

# --- Serving (see src/server.ts, which documents every variable on this list) ---
# PORT/HOST decide where the API listens. HOST defaults to 127.0.0.1: this process serves one
# person's entire financial history, and loopback is the only bind that needs no further
# thought. PGLITE_DATA_DIR is where the development database persists when DATABASE_URL is
# unset — deliberately on disk, so a restart and `scripts/seed-dev-data.ts` see the same rows.
PORT=4000
HOST=127.0.0.1
PGLITE_DATA_DIR=./local-data/pglite-dev
# web/'s origin. Never a wildcard: the session cookie is sent cross-origin only because the
# response names one origin and allows credentials.
CORS_ORIGIN=http://localhost:3000
# true/false. Unset defaults to **on** for any bind that is not loopback, so exposing this on a
# network interface is authenticated by default and turning that off has to be typed out.
AUTH_REQUIRED=

# --- Optical receipt extraction (see ADR-0051, docs/security/security-model.md) ---
# A generated PDF's text layer is always read locally, on this machine, configured or not.
# A *photographed* receipt has no text layer, and the only way this build can read one is a
# multimodal model — which means the document's bytes leaving the local boundary. That is off
# unless this says true, and having ANTHROPIC_API_KEY set is deliberately not enough: a model
# configured for classification is not consent to send it a picture of a receipt.
AI_DOCUMENT_VISION=

# --- Automated notification intake (see audit row 12, src/api/intake-routes.ts) ---
# The shared secret a mail rule or a phone shortcut sends as `Authorization: Bearer <token>`
# to POST /api/intake/messages, which appends bank SMS and UPI push notifications as immutable
# evidence. Leave blank and that endpoint refuses every request: an unconfigured intake route
# standing open would be a stranger's write path into a person's evidence table.
INTAKE_FORWARDING_TOKEN=

# --- Proof-pack message transport (see ADR-0053, audit row 42) ---
# A WhatsApp Cloud API access token and the sending number's phone-number id. Both are needed
# together. Leave them blank and a pack can still be previewed, reviewed and copied — which
# sends nothing — while the send action states, before anything is typed, that no transport is
# configured. Sending is always a separate act after the recipient/content/evidence review,
# and it never records a settlement.
WHATSAPP_ACCESS_TOKEN=
WHATSAPP_PHONE_NUMBER_ID=

# --- Live bank/card balances (see ADR-0054, audit row 37) ---
# An HTTPS JSON endpoint that answers a POST of {"accountRefs":[...]} with a balance per
# account, and a bearer token for it. No Indian retail bank offers this to an individual
# directly — the real paths are an Account Aggregator consent flow or a self-hosted bridge, and
# both terminate in an endpoint like this one, which is what this integrates with.
#
# Leave blank and every read is recorded as INCOMPLETE rather than as an empty success: "we
# could not check" and "we checked and there was nothing" are different claims.
#
# A reading is never a reconciliation boundary, configured or not. A boundary is a statement
# balance you evidenced; a reading is a second opinion shown beside it, with its own timestamp
# and staleness. Nothing here can make an unaccounted delta verified.
BALANCE_PROVIDER_URL=
BALANCE_PROVIDER_TOKEN=
# Optional. A stable id and a human label recorded on every reading, so a figure can be traced
# to what produced it after the endpoint has moved on.
BALANCE_PROVIDER_ID=
BALANCE_PROVIDER_LABEL=
